WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:05.179
This briefing is Book 09 of the
Federal Modernization Workbook,

3
00:00:05.179 --> 00:00:06.762
Network and Transport.

4
00:00:06.762 --> 00:00:11.885
It's about moving branch traffic off the
long hairpin through a distant data center,

5
00:00:11.885 --> 00:00:15.226
without turning a latency
gain into a compliance loss.

6
00:00:15.226 --> 00:00:19.100
Faster and governed are different
things, and the branch needs both.

7
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.914
We'll go in four steps: why
physics decides the architecture,

8
00:00:22.914 --> 00:00:26.650
what has to change, who owns the
network, and how to get there.

9
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.462
Here's the short version up front.

10
00:00:28.462 --> 00:00:30.799
No product shortens a fiber path.

11
00:00:30.799 --> 00:00:34.287
So buy transport on physics,
and govern it as compliance.

12
00:00:34.287 --> 00:00:35.930
Let's start with the physics.
